From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:30:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Send the mentions the Messaging app picked

When the user picks people to mention, the transport puts them on the
conversation as "webos-send-mentions" just before serv_send_im or
serv_chat_send, as "<id>\x1f<name>" records joined by "\x1e", and the
text has "@<name>" for each. It removes the value again when the call
returns.

send_im did nothing with mentions, so a DM went out with the bare
"@name" text. chat_send only guessed at mentions from the text with
discord_make_mentions, which cannot find a name with a space in it
unless it is two words, nor one it does not know as a user name, alias
or nickname.

Both now turn each "@<name>" of a record into a Discord mention,
"<@user id>", before anything else and before any asynchronous step,
so a DM that still has to be created gets them too. The user is found
by the record's id (the buddy name), then by the name the chat shows,
the ways discord_make_mention looks up a typed "@name" (that lookup
moves to a function both use), then by a group DM member's display
name, and last by the id as a user snowflake. A record that resolves
to nobody leaves its text alone. chat_send still runs its own guessing
afterwards on whatever is left.

The rewriting itself is discord_webos_apply_mentions in
webos_helpers.c, with unit tests: the longest name wins and a name
only counts as a whole word, so "@Ann" is not found in "@Anna" or
"me@Ann.example", and a name is also found HTML-escaped.

"webos-send-location" and "webos-send-contact" are left alone: Discord
has no message form of its own for either, and the text the transport
sends already carries them.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
